---
title: Pan-Grilled Chicken Breast
image: https://thatsaladlady.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/01/That_Salad_Lady_Pan_Grilled_Chicken_Recipe-scaled.jpg
servings: 3
prep time: 10 minutes
time required: 25 minutes
nutrition:
  calories: 170 cal
cuisine: American
cook time: 15 minutes
author: Nina Cherie Franklin
course: Main
source: https://thatsaladlady.com/recipes/salad-toppings/perfect-pan-grilled-chicken-breast-recipe/#wpzoom-premium-recipe-card
---

Place the @chicken breasts{2}(boneless, skinless) in a resealable bag. Pound the chicken to an even thickness, about 1/2 inch, starting with the flat side of a meat mallet for consistency and switching to the textured side to tenderize further. A heavy object like a rolling pin works too. 

Pat the tenderized chicken dry with paper towels to remove excess moisture and ensure proper browning.

In a #small bowl{}, mix @kosher salt{1%tsp}, @black pepper{1/2%tsp}(freshly cracked), @garlic powder{1/2%tsp}, and @dried oregano{1/2%tsp}.

Sprinkle the chicken with the seasonings, pressing them into the surface to help them adhere and enhance the flavor. Repeat on the other side.

Heat a #skillet{} over medium-high heat and add @neutral oil{1%tbsp}. Spread the oil evenly across the pan and heat until it shimmers but doesn't smoke.

Add the chicken breasts to the hot pan and cook for ~{5-6%minutes} on the first side without moving them. 

Flip and cook for another ~{5-6%minutes}, or until the internal temperature reaches 165°F (74°C).

Transfer to a preheated oven at 400°F (200°C) and bake for ~{10-15%minutes}, or until fully cooked.

Remove the chicken from the oven and let it rest for ~{5%minutes}. 

> This step allows the juices to redistribute, resulting in tender, flavorful meat.

Slice the chicken into strips or cubes, depending on your salad needs.